<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My DevSecOps Portfolio</title>
</head>

<body id="top">

    <!-- Header and Navigation -->
    <header>
        <h1>My DevSecOps Portfolio</h1>
        <p>Learning Linux, Networking, Frontend Development and DevSecOps</p>

        <nav>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="#home">Home</a></li>
                <li><a href="#about">About</a></li>
                <li><a href="#skills">Skills</a></li>
                <li><a href="#projects">Projects</a></li>
                <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
            </ul>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main>

        <!-- Home Section -->
        <section id="home">
            <h2>Welcome to My Portfolio</h2>

            <p>
                Welcome to my first personal portfolio website!
                I am currently learning technology and developing
                practical skills in Linux, networking, web development
                and DevSecOps.
            </p>

            <p>
                My goal is to understand how websites, computer systems
                and secure software environments work.
            </p>

            <a href="#about">Learn More About Me</a>
        </section>

        <!-- About Section -->
        <section id="about">
            <h2>About Me</h2>

            <p>
                I am a technology learner interested in computer systems,
                software development and cybersecurity.
            </p>

            <p>
                I am currently building my technical knowledge through
                a DevSecOps internship.
            </p>

            <p>
                During my training, I have explored Linux commands,
                file permissions, Bash scripting, computer networking
                and SSH connectivity.
            </p>

            <p>
                I am learning DevSecOps to understand how development,
                security and operations work together.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Skills Section -->
        <section id="skills">
            <h2>Technical Skills</h2>

            <p>Some technologies and concepts I am currently learning:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Linux Fundamentals</li>
                <li>Bash Scripting</li>
                <li>Computer Networking</li>
                <li>SSH Connectivity</li>
                <li>HTML5</li>
                <li>Git and GitHub</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Projects Section -->
        <section id="projects">
            <h2>My Projects</h2>

            <article>
                <h3>Project 1: Linux System Information Script</h3>

                <p>
                    Created a Bash script to collect and display
                    important system information on a Linux machine.
                </p>

                <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Linux, Bash Scripting, Terminal</p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Learning Outcome:</strong>
                    Learned how to automate basic system information
                    collection using Bash.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>Project 2: Linux Networking and SSH Lab</h3>

                <p>
                    Practiced Linux networking commands and explored
                    IP addresses, network interfaces and SSH concepts.
                </p>

                <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Linux, Networking, SSH</p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Learning Outcome:</strong>
                    Improved understanding of network configuration
                    and remote connectivity.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>Project 3: Personal Portfolio Website</h3>

                <p>
                    Developed a personal portfolio webpage using
                    HTML5 to present technical skills and projects.
                </p>

                <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> HTML5, VS Code, Firefox</p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Learning Outcome:</strong>
                    Learned HTML document structure, semantic elements,
                    navigation and forms.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <!-- Contact Section -->
        <section id="contact">
            <h2>Contact Me</h2>

            <p>You can use the form below to send a message.</p>

            <form action="#" method="post">

                <div>
                    <label for="name">Name:</label>
                    <input
                        type="text"
                        id="name"
                        name="name"
                        placeholder="Enter your name"
                        required>
                </div>

                <br>

                <div>
                    <label for="email">Email:</label>
                    <input
                        type="email"
                        id="email"
                        name="email"
                        placeholder="Enter your email"
                        required>
                </div>

                <br>

                <div>
                    <label for="message">Message:</label>
                    <textarea
                        id="message"
                        name="message"
                        rows="5"
                        placeholder="Write your message"
                        required></textarea>
                </div>

                <br>

                <button type="submit">Submit Message</button>

            </form>

            <p>
                Note: This is a demonstration form.
                It does not send or store messages yet.
            </p>
        </section>

    </main>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
        <p>My DevSecOps Portfolio</p>
        <p>&copy; 2026 My Portfolio. All rights reserved.</p>
        <a href="#top">Back to Top</a>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
